messages:
maria: Quick heads-up — opening a TF PR to reduce web-frontend Deployment replicas 6 -> 3 during off-peak to save cost. Can someone quick-check PDB/HPA interactions and whether this will cause disruption on node drains? PR has plan snippet below.

maria: ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_deployment" "web" {
  spec {
    replicas = 3
    strategy {
      type = "RollingUpdate"
      rolling_update {
        max_surge = "25%"
        max_unavailable = "25%"
      }
    }
  }
}

resource "kubernetes_pod_disruption_budget" "web_pdb" {
  spec {
    min_available = 2
    selector {
      match_labels = { app = "web" }
    }
  }
}
```

ajay: quick read — lowering replicas is ok but watch HPA min/max. What's the HPA minReplicas? if HPA min is 1 you could drop below PDB minAvailable during aggressive scale events.

ajay: suggestion: set HPA minReplicas = 2 and change max_unavailable to "1" (absolute) on the Deployment rollingUpdate so we never make more than one pod unavailable at a time.

leo: are we applying to prod directly or doing a canary in prod? which clusters/regions?

maria: prod/us-central only, low-traffic window sunday 02:00-04:00. PR: https://git.internal/r/redwood/web/merge_requests/3921 — plan shows no instance replacement, just replica count change.

sophie: also consider using partitioned rollout so pods are updated in two waves. partition = 50% then 100% reduces blast radius if something unexpected happens.

sophie: and check podDisruptionBudget vs nodePool autoscaler: node drains during upgrades might conflict with PDB if minAvailable is too high.

infra-bot: Terraform plan (summary):
 - kubernetes_deployment.web: update in-place (replicas: 6 -> 3)
 - kubernetes_pod_disruption_budget.web_pdb: update (min_available: 3 -> 2)
Plan: 0 to add, 2 to change, 0 to destroy.

ajay: +1 to partitioned/staggered rollout and HPA min=2. If you want minimal risk, keep replicas=4 rather than 3 for one-week trial.

maria: good call. i'll update the PR: set HPA minReplicas=2, rollingUpdate.max_unavailable=1, add annotation for rollout.partition=50 then deploy. i'll also change replicas -> 4 for a week to monitor.

maria: tagging ops for a quick schedule approval: @leo @sophie — can you ack timing and I'll merge the updated PR tomorrow? :thumbsup:

leo: ack. sunday window looks fine from infra side.

sophie: ack. i'll add a dashboard watch for p95 latency and pod churn alerts.

maria: thanks all — i'll push the PR patch and ping here when it's ready for merge.
